      "headline": "The Universal Inspection Template",
      "keyInsight": "Imagine a master detective who uses the exact same four-step checklist on every single crime scene. That is the famous Satipatthana Refrain. It repeats like a musical chorus after every single meditation practice in the ancient text. Why? Because the human brain loves to get lost in the story of what is happening. If your shoulder aches, you immediately invent a drama about bad chairs or getting old. The refrain pulls you out of the soap opera and plugs you directly into raw data. You observe the sensation inside yourself, then you recognize that everyone else feels it too. You watch how sensations arrive like waves and wash away like foam. Finally, you stop clinging to the experience like personal property. The secret genius of the refrain is that it treats every thought, emotion, and muscle twitch like weather passing through an open sky.",
      "content": "In music, a catchy chorus keeps bringing you back to the core theme of the song. The Satipatthana Refrain is the mental chorus of mindfulness. No matter what you are observing\u2014your breath, a fiery emotion, or a daydream\u2014you run it through the exact same mental inspection loop. It turns every chaotic life event into a simple, observable experiment.\n\nFirst, you look internally at your own experience, then externally at the world around you. You realize that your stress or joy is not a weird personal curse. It is just human biology in action, shared by every person stuck in traffic next to you. Next, you observe how things start, how they peak, and how they dissolve. You watch anger build like a summer thunderstorm, dump its rain, and vanish into cool air.\n\nFinally, you practice bare ownership. You treat thoughts and body feelings the way an air traffic controller treats passing jets. You identify their altitude and speed, but you never run outside to jump onto their wings. You remain unattached and free, letting everything flow through without sticking to the walls of your mind.",
